        "created_at": "2019-04-30T10:07:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\"WELCOME TO WHO'S TURN IS IT ANYWAY!&nbsp; WHERE THE PLAN'S MADE UP AND THE HP DOESN'T MATTER!\"</p>\n<p>No, no, that's a different one-shot. I designed it, and I THINK I proposed it to MigrantP, but I don't remember. It's a Vengeance game with AA, Scholar, La Comodora, Guise, and Action Hero Stuntman against Friction, Baron Blade, La Capitan, Miss Information, and Sergeant Steel in the Temple of Zhu-Long. The decks, of course, are stacked for maximized turn-mixing shenanigans.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>... But enough about that.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This was one of the easiest games I've ever played, period. Everyone was at mostly-full health, and I had to acticeac attack the Scholar so he could heal and make use of his L-L-L-E-E-E setup. Tachyon hurt herself a bit, and AA got hit by the Rockslide once, but that's it.</p>",
