      {
        "id": 226701,
        "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-04-30T14:47:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Super easy mint, with everyone within 1-2 hp of full, except for Tachyon because I kept out Pushing the Limits longer than I really needed to. Even she was around 20 though.<br>\n<br>\nSoooooooooo much card draw. Everyone had pretty much their entire deck in hand by the end, which suited me fine. Always had exactly what I needed, although I didn't really need all that much. Played Don't Dismiss Anything 5-6 times through La Comodora's power, could have done the same with Takedown if I wanted to lock it down even more. Decided to go with Tachyon as my damage dealer, and she worked pretty well.<br>\n<br>\nOne \"Cheeky Bastard!\" play I found in this one shot: If Tachyon has an empty deck but full of Burst card and Lightspeed Barrage trash, and La Comodora has 3 copies of Harnessed Anomaly in hand, Tachyon can play another 3 Lightspeed Barrages on the same turn :) Comodora puts Barrage in Tachyon's empty deck, \"shuffles\", then plays the top card, then Comodora chooses to play another Anomaly to repeat.<br>\n<br>\n~Komori</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:00:43.538Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
